---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PUBS } from '../../data/publications';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const pub = (id: string) => PUBS.find((p) => p.id === id)!;
const last = (p: (typeof PUBS)[number]) => p.events[p.events.length - 1].date.replace(/-/g, '.');
const ex = Object.fromEntries((await getCollection('projects')).filter((p) => p.data.kind === 'research').map((p) => [p.id, p]));
const m = (id: string, i = 0) => ex[id]?.data.metrics[i];
---
<Base title="Research — Hyeonmin Jeon" active="research">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="list-head">
      <div><h1>Research</h1><p>The questions I am working on, each with the experiments behind it and where the write-up stands. Review stages and manuscript numbers live on the <a href="/publications/">Publications</a> page; applied and engineering work lives under <a href="/projects/">Projects</a>.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="now">
      <div><span class="e">The question</span><span class="t">How much of a selection guarantee survives when the simulation's input model was learned from data?</span><span class="s">Every thread below is one way of asking it, and the working answer is the same: a model that carries the problem's own uncertainty, in its architecture or in its batch structure, becomes a surrogate through which the decision can be controlled and adapted. A learned scenario generator, a learned prior, a fitted input distribution, a learned arrival process, an early-life battery predictor.</span></div>
      <div><span class="e">Where it stands</span><span class="t">Two papers under review, two working papers, and experiment lines toward the next</span><span class="s">Review stages live on Publications; code and results on each thread's experiment page.</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sec-h" style="margin-top:30px"><h2>Ongoing</h2><span class="hnote">six threads — two papers under review, two working papers, and experiments meant to become one</span></div>
    <ul class="feat threads">
      <li>
        <a class="card" href="/research/diffusion-scenarios/"><img src="/projects/diffusion-scenarios/media/architecture.png" alt="CASE architecture: representation, embeddings, denoiser and sampling" loading="lazy"></a>
        <div class="kick"><span>Thread 1 · generative scenario engines</span><span class={`status ${pub('case').stageClass}`}>{pub('case').stage} · ESWA</span></div>
        <a class="t" href="/research/diffusion-scenarios/">Conditional diffusion as a portfolio-risk scenario engine</a>
        <p class="k">Topic: generating joint return scenarios for many assets at once, and judging the generator by the risk decision made on it. Method: a conditional diffusion transformer re-conditioned each day; its VaR/ES reserves are scored against realised losses across several portfolio books. TailFlow repeats the question on a synthetic market where the true risk is known.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="/research/diffusion-scenarios/">paper · CASE <small>1st author · {last(pub('case'))}</small></a><a href="/research/tailflow/">experiments · TailFlow</a></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="card" href="/research/finphasor/"><img src="/projects/finphasor/media/architecture.png" alt="FinPhasor architecture: scale-conditioned cross-attention read-out and Grad-CAM attribution" loading="lazy"></a>
        <div class="kick"><span>Thread 2 · timing in the cross-section</span><span class={`status ${pub('finphasor').stageClass}`}>{pub('finphasor').stageShort ?? pub('finphasor').stage} · ESWA</span></div>
        <a class="t" href="/research/finphasor/">Phase-preserving measurement of when stocks reprice</a>
        <p class="k">Topic: when stocks reprice after the same news, which can be weeks apart. Method: predict each stock's future complex wavelet scalogram, keep the phase that a magnitude-only forecast throws away, and use it to rank the cross-section; Grad-CAM shows which scales the ranking relies on.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="/research/finphasor/">paper · FinPhasor <small>1st author · {last(pub('finphasor'))}</small></a></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="card" href="/research/model-uncertainty-priors/"><img src="/projects/model-uncertainty-priors/media/posterior_thumb.jpg" alt="Posterior over all 1,024 factor subsets: exact, flow density route, and sampling route collapsing" loading="lazy"></a>
        <div class="kick"><span>Thread 3 · learned surrogates for Bayesian model selection</span><span class="status s-wip">Working paper · experimenting</span></div>
        <a class="t" href="/research/model-uncertainty-priors/">A learned prior as a surrogate — what its density buys, and what a sampler costs</a>
        <p class="k">Topic: the prior in Bayesian factor selection, and what changes when it is learned instead of fixed. Method: replace the mixture-of-g prior with a normalizing flow that keeps an explicit density, check it against the exact posterior over models, compare it with a density-free GAN prior, then tune and re-tune the flow with Bayesian optimisation and track both the selected model and its model-uncertainty measure.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="/research/model-uncertainty-priors/">experiments &amp; write-up</a></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="card" href="/research/rs-lab/"><img src="/projects/rs-lab/media/thumb.jpg" alt="rs-lab: attained probability of correct selection against the nominal level" loading="lazy"></a>
        <div class="kick"><span>Thread 4 · selection with guarantees</span><span class="status s-wip">Experiments · toward a paper</span></div>
        <a class="t" href="/research/rs-lab/">Ranking &amp; selection when the simulation's input model is itself fitted</a>
        <p class="k">Topic: choosing the best of several simulated systems when the simulation's input distribution was itself estimated from data. Method: implement and verify standard procedures (KN, feasibility determination, recycled observations), then swap fitted and generative input models underneath them and measure what happens to the probability-of-correct-selection guarantee.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="/research/rs-lab/">rs-lab</a><a href="/research/input-uncertainty-select/">Input-Uncertainty Select</a></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="card" href="/projects/exchange-queueing/"><img src="/projects/exchange-queueing/media/queue.jpg" alt="Exchange queue: arrivals, servers and the queueing delay against the 100 ms SLA" loading="lazy"></a>
        <div class="kick"><span>Thread 5 · capacity under learned arrival uncertainty</span><span class="status s-wip">Working paper · experimenting</span></div>
        <a class="t" href="/projects/exchange-queueing/">Sizing an exchange matching queue when the arrival process is learned</a>
        <p class="k">Topic: how many servers an exchange's matching engine needs when order arrivals are bursty and uncertain. Method: a Bayesian batch-arrival model fitted to real BTC/USDT tick data, a simulated queue with a latency SLA, and a learned surrogate of the SLA probability so the capacity decision can be re-solved every minute.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="/projects/exchange-queueing/">experiments &amp; write-up</a><a href="/publications/">working paper</a></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="card" href="/research/battery-protocol-select/"><img src="/projects/battery-protocol-select/media/thumb.jpg" alt="Battery capacity fade to end of life: 124 cells, three highlighted" loading="lazy"></a>
        <div class="kick"><span>Thread 6 · an expensive test and a learned surrogate</span><span class="status s-wip">Experiment · new domain</span></div>
        <a class="t" href="/research/battery-protocol-select/">Choosing a fast-charging protocol when the early-life prediction is uncertain</a>
        <p class="k">Topic: choosing a fast-charging protocol when testing each one takes months of cycling. Method: an early-life cycle-life predictor that reports its own uncertainty serves as a surrogate, and a sequential ranking-and-selection procedure decides which protocols to keep testing; a physics-based degradation simulation checks where cells collapse.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="/research/battery-protocol-select/">experiments &amp; write-up</a><a href="/research/battery-degradation-sim/">battery degradation, simulated <small>where a cell collapses</small></a></div>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="sec-h" id="manuscripts" style="margin-top:44px;scroll-margin-top:24px"><h2>Manuscripts</h2><span class="hnote">first-author papers under review, working papers on their way to submission, then lab papers where I am second or third author; review stages on <a href="/publications/">Publications</a></span></div>
    <ul class="rows rl">
      <li><a href="/research/diffusion-scenarios/">
        <span class="d">{pub('case').year}</span>
        <div><div class="t">{pub('case').title}</div>
          <div class="k">Diffusion-based scenario generation for portfolio risk: a conditional diffusion transformer generates joint multi-asset returns, and is evaluated by the VaR/ES reserves set on its scenarios rather than by sample realism.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class={`status ${pub('case').stageClass}`}>{pub('case').stage} · ESWA</span><span>1st author · {last(pub('case'))}</span></div></a></li>
      <li><a href="/research/finphasor/">
        <span class="d">{pub('finphasor').year}</span>
        <div><div class="t">{pub('finphasor').title}</div>
          <div class="k">Measuring when stocks reprice: forecasting complex wavelet scalograms keeps the phase of price moves, which a magnitude-only forecast discards, and the phase is used to rank the cross-section by repricing timing.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class={`status ${pub('finphasor').stageClass}`}>{pub('finphasor').stageShort ?? pub('finphasor').stage} · ESWA</span><span>1st author · {last(pub('finphasor'))}</span></div></a></li>
      <li><a href="/research/model-uncertainty-priors/">
        <span class="d">now</span>
        <div><div class="t">Learned Surrogate Priors for Bayesian Model Selection: Density, Uncertainty, and the Cost of a Sampler</div>
          <div class="k">Learned priors for Bayesian factor selection: a normalizing flow with an explicit density replaces the mixture-of-g prior, is checked against the exact posterior over models and tuned by Bayesian optimisation.</div>
          <ol class="stages"><li class="done">Idea</li><li class="cur">Experiments</li><li>Drafting</li><li>Internal review</li><li>Submission</li></ol></div>
        <div class="r"><span class="status s-wip">Working paper</span><span>1st author · not yet submitted</span></div></a></li>
      <li><a href="/projects/exchange-queueing/">
        <span class="d">now</span>
        <div><div class="t">Bayesian Capacity Sizing for an Exchange Matching Queue under Over-Dispersed Arrivals</div>
          <div class="k">Capacity sizing for an exchange matching queue: a Bayesian batch-arrival model of real tick data and a learned surrogate of the queue's latency SLA, used to choose the number of servers.</div>
          <ol class="stages"><li class="done">Idea</li><li class="cur">Experiments</li><li>Drafting</li><li>Internal review</li><li>Submission</li></ol></div>
        <div class="r"><span class="status s-wip">Working paper</span><span>1st author · not yet submitted</span></div></a></li>
      <li><div class="row3">
        <span class="d">{pub('convfactornet').year}</span>
        <div><div class="t">ConvFactorNet — deep convolutional factor prediction with explainable AI</div>
          <div class="k">A CNN reads the whole cross-section at one date and emits latent factors instead of returns; betas come from OLS on those factors. Grad-CAM then says which of the 110 inputs the factors were built from, and re-training on only those inputs improves the strategy. Korean equities, 2015–2023.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class={`status ${pub('convfactornet').stageClass}`}>{pub('convfactornet').stage}</span><span>2nd author · {last(pub('convfactornet'))}</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="row3">
        <span class="d">{pub('neif').year}</span>
        <div><div class="t">N-EIF — enhanced index fund via genetic algorithm, volume–price index and LSTM dueling DQN</div>
          <div class="k">Two-phase enhanced indexing: a genetic algorithm builds the tracking basket, then a volume–price regime indicator and a recurrent dueling DQN must agree before a trade happens. The contribution worth reading is the decomposition of how much each layer is worth — done twice, by two methods that agree.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class={`status ${pub('neif').stageClass}`}>{pub('neif').stage}</span><span>3rd author · {last(pub('neif'))}</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="sec-h" id="completed" style="margin-top:44px;scroll-margin-top:24px"><h2>Completed</h2><span class="hnote">presented, submitted to a challenge, or closed with a report</span></div>
    <ul class="rows rl">
      <li><a href="/research/isf2025-solar-forecasting/">
        <span class="d">2025.07</span>
        <div><div class="t">A Study for Forecasting Solar Energy Power Generation — ISF 2025, Beijing</div>
          <div class="k">Hourly solar generation in Seoul with a hybrid CNN–LSTM–Transformer against ARIMA, TimesFM and CNN–LSTM; when only 15 days (360 h) of history exist, diffusion-generated synthetic series stacked on the real data. Joint work with SAS Institute and the University of Seoul; talk delivered 2025.07.01.</div>
          <div class="pm"><span><b>0.304</b> one-day-ahead RMSE vs 0.392 CNN–LSTM, 3.19 TimesFM, 4.2 ARIMA</span><span><b>2.91 → 1.97</b> CNN–LSTM RMSE with synthetic data on 15 days (360 h) of history (hybrid 2.97 → 2.00)</span></div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class="status s-acc">Presented · talk</span><span>co-author · slides on the page</span></div></a></li>
      <li><a href="/projects/tiny-yolo-quantization/">
        <span class="d">2024</span>
        <div><div class="t">Light-weighting Tiny YOLOv3 — graduation thesis (졸업논문)</div>
          <div class="k">Int8 quantization with layer fusion, symmetric scales in the body and asymmetric before the detection heads; total footprint 1.6 GB → 100 MB (weight file 4× smaller), inference 22–64 % faster from a Raspberry Pi 4 to an RTX 3080, mAP −2.78 pt on PASCAL VOC. With S. Kim and H. Kim, advised by Prof. Minhyeok Lee.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class="status s-done">Graduation thesis · 2024</span><span>team of three</span></div></a></li>
      <li><div class="row3">
        <span class="d">2024</span>
        <div><div class="t">Enhancing Portfolio Optimization with Latent Diffusion Models — a comparative study with AC-GAN</div>
          <div class="k">A latent diffusion model and a predictive AC-GAN as classifiers of expected return and risk on S&amp;P 500 daily prices 1990–2024; the diffusion-conditioned portfolio kept higher returns and a smaller drawdown under uncertainty cut-offs. With M. Lee, GAIL. Manuscript, 2024.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class="status s-plan">Manuscript</span><span>1st author</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="row3">
        <span class="d">2024</span>
        <div><div class="t">Personalized Sleep Score Prediction Model Using a Lifelog Dataset</div>
          <div class="k">Smartwatch lifelog data (Withings / Empatica) to nightly sleep-score prediction — ETRI Human Understanding AI Paper Challenge, 2024.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class="status s-acc">Submitted · ETRI challenge</span><span>1st author</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="row3">
        <span class="d">2023.11</span>
        <div><div class="t">Dealing with the Imbalanced-Data Problem with a Diffusion Model</div>
          <div class="k">Diffusion-model oversampling for a credit-card fraud dataset, compared with random over/under-sampling and SMOTE. Korea Institute of Communication Sciences (KICS) fall conference 2023, with M. Lee.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class="status s-acc">Presented · KICS</span><span>1st author</span></div></div></li>
      <li><a href="/projects/eco-route-rl/">
        <span class="d">2023.04 – 12</span>
        <div><div class="t">Green-Navi — RL for fuel-optimal urban routing (team lead)</div>
          <div class="k">Undergraduate research team in the Carbon-Neutral ESG Practical-Problem Research Group at Chung-Ang University (Green AI track, MSIT / NRF <i>Field-Linked Future-Leading Talent</i> programme). Fuel and CO₂ measured on candidate Seoul routes in AIMSUN, then a routing policy; presented at the research fair on 2023.11.02. Rebuilt with simulation methodology as Eco-Route RL.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class="status s-acc">Presented · research fair</span><span>team lead · → Eco-Route RL</span></div></a></li>
      <li><div class="row3">
        <span class="d">2023 – 2024</span>
        <div><div class="t">3D point-cloud classification</div>
          <div class="k">Lab project at GAIL — the first hands-on work with vision and generative models, which led to the diffusion-oversampling paper.</div></div>
        <div class="r"><span class="status s-done">Lab project</span><span>GAIL, 2022.12 – 2024.12</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
